{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d and 2 d texture painting views 3 d and 2 d texture painting views","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","fileName":"3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D and 2D Texture Painting Views","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:18\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Texture Painting Workflow]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Texture Painting Workflow","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d and 2 d texture painting views 3 d and 2 d texture painting views","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","fileName":"3D and 2D Texture Painting Views.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D and 2D Texture Painting Views","heading":"3D and 2D Texture Painting Views","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender can paint an image through the textured 3D mesh in the Viewport or directly on the flattened canvas in the Image Editor. Both views modify the same pixels through the active UV mapping.\n\nThe 3D view provides surface context and hides much of the island fragmentation, while the 2D view exposes seams, padding, and exact image placement. Moving between them helps separate appearance on the object from organization in texture space.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Texture Painting Workflow","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full No